.Dd 2025-09-30
.Dt RAND_EGD 3ossl
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm RAND_egd ,
.Nm RAND_egd_bytes ,
.Nm RAND_query_egd_bytes
.Nd query entropy gathering daemon
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In openssl/rand.h
.Ft int
.Fo RAND_egd_bytes
.Fa "const char *path"
.Fa "int num"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo RAND_egd
.Fa "const char *path"
.Fc
.Ft int
.Fo RAND_query_egd_bytes
.Fa "const char *path"
.Fa "unsigned char *buf"
.Fa "int num"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
On older platforms without a good source of randomness such as
.Qo Li /dev/urandom Qc ,
it is possible to query an Entropy Gathering Daemon (EGD) over a local
socket to obtain randomness and seed the OpenSSL RNG. The protocol used
is defined by the EGDs available at
.Lk http://egd.sourceforge.net/
or
.Lk http://prngd.sourceforge.net .
.Pp
.Fn RAND_egd_bytes
requests
.Fa num
bytes of randomness from an EGD at the specified socket
.Fa path ,
and passes the data it receives into
.Xr RAND_add 3 .
.Fn RAND_egd
is equivalent to
.Fn RAND_egd_bytes
with
.Fa num
set to 255.
.Pp
.Fn RAND_query_egd_bytes
requests
.Fa num
bytes of randomness from an EGD at the specified socket
.Fa path ,
where
.Fa num
must be less than 256. If
.Fa buf
is
.Dv NULL ,
it is equivalent to
.Fn RAND_egd_bytes .
If
.Fa buf
is not
.Dv NULL ,
then the data is copied to the buffer and
.Xr RAND_add 3
is not called.
.Pp
OpenSSL can be configured at build time to try to use the EGD for
seeding automatically.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn RAND_egd
and
.Fn RAND_egd_bytes
return the number of bytes read from the daemon on success, or -1 if the
connection failed or the daemon did not return enough data to fully seed
the PRNG.
.Pp
.Fn RAND_query_egd_bytes
returns the number of bytes read from the daemon on success, or -1 if
the connection failed.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr RAND_add 3 ,
.Xr RAND_bytes 3 ,
.Xr RAND 7
